  "recap": "The Base Invaders dropped a high-scoring affair to the Giants, 18–24, in a game that saw plenty of action at the plate on both sides. With 34 hits spread across 12 players reaching base, the offense was far from quiet — the runs just weren't quite enough to keep pace with a Giants squad that had a big night of their own. Brandon led the way with a 5-for-7 effort and 3 RBI, while Keith was equally relentless going 5-for-6 with an RBI, giving the Invaders a pair of players who refused to make easy outs all game long. Sean was locked in as well, going a perfect 4-for-4 with a team-high 4 RBI, and Mark chipped in a 2-for-3 line with 2 RBI to keep the middle of the order producing. Alexander added a 2-for-3 night with an RBI of his own, rounding out a lineup that genuinely brought it. A 6-run deficit in a game this offensively active stings, but the Base Invaders showed they can hit with anyone — the focus now turns to tightening things up on the other side of the ball.",
